/*&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&
Errors.Inc:

Author: Rajendra Shah

This file contains list of

	o Constants for error numbers used by various pieces of GRiD Server and 
	  Grid Central related software.  

	o errors used otherwise on compass and usually found in Os.Error.Inc.

    o Errors used in boot up Diagnostics.


Only few of the errors listed here have a descriptive message in the 
'@SystemErrors~text~' file used on Compass and GRiD Server.  Those errors have
a '$' in front of their comments.   These are the errors which may be seen by 
applications running on Compass.

Rest of the errors are used internally by server related software packages.  
This packages use these errors to display their own messages, or log them to 
the diagnostic display and/or the 'Errorlog~text~' file.

You many find in this file

	- error codes that are never used.
	- multiple error codes for the same kind of error.
	- an error code that does not make sense.

As you notice them, please let me know so that it can be cleaned up in future.


GRiD Server Developers Please note:

This file is organised in the form of a a plm include file.  If you wish to use
only the GRiD Server & GRiD central related constants, you can simply include 
the file if you do not use a compilation variable named 'IncludeOsConstants'.
If you also want to use the constants for normal compass error (those usually found
in Os.Error.Inc) include this file after setting a compile time variable named 
'IncludeOsConstants' as follows:

		$SET (IncludeOsConstants)
		$INCLUDE (`w`Incs`Errors.Inc)

&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&&*/


